a **pointer and workflow contract**. Read the `AGENTS.md` nearest the code\nyou are about to touch.\n\n## Where things live\n\n| Path | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `client/` | Godot 4.7 project: `project.godot`, `mind.gdextension`, `.tscn` scenes, GDScript UI, shaders, third-party addons, plus the Rust workspace in `client/rust/`. |\n| `client/rust/` | Cargo workspace — `mind-core`, `mind-headless`, `mind-gdext`, `mind-stdb`, `mind-tools`, `mind-atlas`, `mind-macros`, `mind-derive`. Implements essentially all behavior. |\n| `server/` | SpacetimeDB module crate (`mindustry_godot`) and its publish / bindings-drift tooling. |\n| `parity/` | Cross-cutting verification oracle: registries, sha256-pinned goldens, JVM/source provenance, screenshots, gate reports, mod fixtures. |\n| `tools/` | Developer/CI scripts (`build`, `ci`, `godot`, `parity`, `server`, `sync_scenarios`, `pack`, `regen_goldens`, `mcp-smoke`, …), each as a canonical `.sh`. |\n| `scenarios/` | Canonical headless scenarios; mirrored to the gitignored `client/scenarios/`. |\n| `assets/` | Packed runtime assets (generated by `mind-tools`); `assets-raw/` is the source art. |\n| `bench/` | Recorded performance baselines (`baselines.json`, `editor_baseline.json`). |\n| `docs/` | Operator-facing platform and packaging notes. |\n| `.github/workflows/` | `ci.yml` (push/PR gate) and `parity-nightly.yml`. |\n| `.opencode/skills/playtest/` | In-engine playtest skill: launch flow, node map, MCP recipes. |\n\n## Documentation map\n\n| Guide | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| [`client/AGENTS.md`](client/AGENTS.md) | Godot project tree: scenes, GDScript UI, shaders, addons, manifests, build/run. |\n| [`client/rust/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/AGENTS.md) | Cargo workspace: crate layout, dependency direction, pinned deps, workspace lints, boundaries. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/AGENTS.md) | Godot-free simulation core: full module map, ECS/schedule/checksum, invariants. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/world/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/world/AGENTS.md) | World/terrain: `WorldGrid`, tile ops, construction, generation, behavior families. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/world/blocks/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/world/blocks/AGENTS.md) | Block families: distribution, storage, power, liquid, heat, payloads, defense/turrets, units, autotiling. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/content/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/content/AGENTS.md) | Content framework, dense IDs, registries and the tech tree. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/io/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/io/AGENTS.md) | Persistence: `MGRS` saves, `TypeIO`, entity IO, `JsonIO`, settings, maps, `MSAV` import. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/logic/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/logic/AGENTS.md) | The mlog system: parser, assembler, VM/executor, logic blocks. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/game/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/game/AGENTS.md) | Game/rules orchestration: state, rules, teams, waves, campaign, objectives, fog. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/render/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/render/AGENTS.md) | Godot-free render data: layers, caches, bands, queue, visible-set scan. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/ai/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/ai/AGENTS.md) | Unit AI, pathfinding (flowfields/A*), controllers, RTS, waves, unit harness. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/combat/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/combat/AGENTS.md) | Bullets, damage, fires, lightning, puddles, targeting, view seam. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/ui/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/ui/AGENTS.md) | Godot-free UI builder, view models and manifest ABI. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-core/src/input/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-core/src/input/AGENTS.md) | Input state machine, placement, plan mirror, RTS selection. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-gdext/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-gdext/AGENTS.md) | GDExtension `cdylib`: `Mind*` classes, fixed-step pump, view/input/audio/FX/net/platform glue. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-headless/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-headless/AGENTS.md) | Headless oracle/test-rig: CLI, scenarios, goldens, parity, dedicated server mode. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-stdb/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-stdb/AGENTS.md) | SpacetimeDB client SDK: connector, waves, binders, ordered command relay. |\n| [`client/rust/mind-tools/AGENTS.md`](client/rust/mind-tools/AGENTS.md) | Offline asset-generation and packing pipeline. |\n| [`server/AGENTS.md`](server/AGENTS.md) | SpacetimeDB module + publish/bindings-drift tooling. |\n| [`server/spacetimedb/AGENTS.md`](server/spacetimedb/AGENTS.md) | Module crate internals: relay, chat, admin, campaign, mods, identity, main. |\n| [`parity/AGENTS.md`](parity/AGENTS.md) | Verification oracle: registries, goldens, harness subcommands, authoring rules. |\n| [`tools/AGENTS.md`](tools/AGENTS.md) | Build and verification scripts, `.sh` convention. |\n| [`docs/AGENTS.md`](docs/AGENTS.md) | Platform and packaging notes. |\n\nThird-party addons carry their own docs (e.g.\n`client/addons/open_godot_mcp/AGENTS.md`); do not edit vendor addons unless the task is about\nthe addon itself.\n\n## Build, run, verify\n\nRun from the repo root. The `.sh` scripts are canonical on the Linux dev host and run the\nrelative `cargo` commands below.\n\n## Workflow rules\n\n- **Document current state only.** `AGENTS.md` files, code comments and docs describe how the\n  code works **now**, in the present tense. Never add history or changelog narration — no\n  \"previously\", \"used to\", \"was replaced\", \"now migrated\", \"legacy\", or phase/milestone\n  framing. If a change alters structure, responsibilities or invariants, update the relevant\n  `AGENTS.md` rather than leaving a note about the change.\n- **Stale root artifacts are not sources of truth.** The `*_PLAN.md` files and `old_AGENTS.md`\n  in the repo root are old planning/scratch material. Do not read them for context and do not\n  propagate their roadmap or plan-number language into code, comments or docs.\n- **Respect the crate boundary.** `mind-core` stays Godot-free and tokio-free; `mind-gdext`\n  holds no game rules and only bridges Godot to `mind-core`; GDScript is UI-only and never\n  mutates simulation state. Hosts call into `mind-core`, never the reverse.\n- **Never hand-edit generated files.** SpacetimeDB bindings\n  (`client/rust/mind-stdb/src/module_bindings/`), packed assets under `assets/`, the\n  `client/scenarios/` mirror and generated manifests are produced by tooling and overwritten.\n  Regenerate with the owning script (`server/build.sh`, `tools/pack.sh`, `tools/sync_scenarios.sh`).\n- **Keep paths relative and host-neutral.** Scripts, docs and commands reference files\n  relative to the repo root or to the file that owns them — never an absolute machine\n  path. Host installs are resolved through environment overrides (`GODOT_BIN`, `MINDY_SRC`,\n  `OPEN_GODOT_MCP_BIN`, …), and sibling checkouts (upstream `Mindustry`, `Arc`, `main`) sit\n  alongside the repo and are referenced relatively (`../Mindustry`, `../Arc`, `../../main`).\n- **Keep parity pinned.** Content IDs, `ContentType` ordinals, entity field order, bundle keys\n  and sprite region names are append-only ABI. A change touching a `parity/checksum_registry.json`\n  contributor bumps `CHECKSUM_VERSION` and re-records every golden in the same change.\n- **Verify before finishing.** Run the applicable checks above; use `tools/ci.sh` for a\n  full gate. New files are UTF-8, LF line endings, no BOM, GPL-3.0-only, and cite the ported\n  Mindustry source in the header when they mirror upstream.\n- Godot-first and editor-navigable. Prefer **nodes and scenes declared in `.tscn` files** over trees\n  built in code; a human should be able to open the project in the Godot editor and navigate/inspect\n  the game. Static UI, world scaffolding, autoloads and debug views belong in scenes. When code must\n  instantiate nodes (spawner-produced units/buildings/bullets, pooled FX, data-driven list entries),\n  add a comment at the instantiation site:\n```gdscript\nvar unit = UNIT_SCENE.instantiate()  # code-instantiated: spawned by WaveSpawner at runtime;\n```\n  The comment must give the **specific** reason (“spawned at runtime”, “pooled/high-churn”, “count\n  driven by server rows”) — “easier in code” is not a justification. Rust owns behavior, not scene\n  construction, for static content. Full rule: `HIGH_LEVEL_PLAN.md` §6.6.\n\n</system-reminder>",
